WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Pair the reference and blurred candidate on the same three-dimensional grid, using gain one.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Compute positive local contrast by subtracting a 0.4 millimetre Gaussian background.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Use only the reference to identify tubular support, then split it into weak and strong contrast groups.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Measure shared contrast in each group. Q is 100 times the geometric mean of the two overlap scores.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Q complements PSNR, full-image SSIM and L1. The three controls retain background and structural changes separately.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Measured mouse: extract the local background and positive contrast from GT.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Evaluate the test image on the weak and strong support defined by GT.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Accumulate shared contrast in both groups throughout the 3D volume to obtain the overlap scores.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.000
Measured mouse result: Dweak = 0.7872, Dstrong = 0.8654, Q = 82.53.

